  spread across settings:  ratio 2.39x   NKI 1.02x   torch 2.35x

  -> NKI is INVARIANT across compiler settings (13.82-14.15 ms,
     1.02x spread). **No setting rescues the NKI path.** So the gap is
     not a compiler-flag artifact, which is what this control set out to establish.
     The ratio spread (2.39x) is driven by TORCH moving (2.35x), not NKI.
     Specifically '--target trn2 --lnc 1' makes torch slower (1.708 ms), which flatters the ratio without helping NKI.
     -> The open item is CLOSED for the wall-clock gap. Record it.

  SCOPE LIMIT — read before citing this as settling Findings #25/#26:
    This measures WALL time. At 13.82 ms for 28 calls that is
    0.494 ms/call, which is the post-fix DISPATCH floor — so this run is
    ~97% dispatch and only a few percent device. It therefore establishes that the
    DISPATCH cost is flag-invariant, and does NOT by itself settle whether the
    DEVICE-time gap in #25/#26 depends on flags. For that, profile device time under
    two settings:
      NEURON_CC_FLAGS='--target trn2 --lnc 2' python scripts/run_device_profile_sweep.py \
          --calls 1 28 --ops silu
    and compare against the default-flag profiles via analyse_fusion_barrier.py.

